  "notes": "2021 IRC was never adopted statewide; 2024 IRC/IECC adoption failed in the 2026 legislature (not in force). Snapshot discrepancies (second check: (1) agreed, see settledQuestions): (1) boise-2018-snapshot energy.airLeakageACH50=5 is not supported: Idaho only added a visual-inspection option to R402.4.1.2; IECC 2018 base for zone 5 is 3 ACH50 (the '20% of homes tested from 7/1/2021' note was not found in the current rule text). (2) R313.2 one-/two-family sprinklers, R302.13, R301.2.1.2, R322.1.10 deleted; exceptions #2 of R314.2.2/R315.2.2 (alterations) deleted; R303.4 whole-house mechanical ventilation per M1505.4 required; R602.10 allows R602.12 or APA SR-102; none change a tracked number. (3) Snapshot's 'Idaho added NEC 210.52(C)(4)' (receptacle up to 12 in below counter if overhang <=6 in) is confirmed; it does not change elec.counterReceptacleMaxAbove in a fixed way. (4) Idaho Zone 6 differs (U-0.30, ceiling R-49, slab 4 ft) but is not needed here."
}
